community a harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of age, body
size, visible or invisible disability, ethnicity, sex characteristics, gender
identity and expression, level of experience, education, socio-economic status,
nationality, personal appearance, race, caste, color, religion, or sexual
identity and orientation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We pledge to act and interact in ways that contribute to an open, welcoming,
diverse, inclusive, and healthy community.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Troubleshooting</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/help/troubleshooting/</link><pubDate>Wed, 12 Nov 2025 15:22:20 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/help/troubleshooting/</guid><description>&lt;div class="alert alert-warning d-flex" role="alert"&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex-shrink-1 alert-icon"&gt;
 &lt;span class="material-icons size-20 me-2"&gt;
 warning
 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="w-100"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Caution&lt;/strong&gt; - This documentation is in progress&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id="troubleshooting"&gt;Troubleshooting &lt;a href="#troubleshooting" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This section provides solutions to common issues you may encounter while using &lt;strong&gt;ETLX&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Because ETLX is &lt;strong&gt;declarative&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;SQL-first&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;configuration-driven&lt;/strong&gt;, most problems are not runtime crashes but &lt;strong&gt;execution decisions&lt;/strong&gt;: blocks not running, steps being skipped, or conditions preventing execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important mental model:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
If ETLX executed &lt;em&gt;anything&lt;/em&gt;, it was logged.&lt;br&gt;
If it did &lt;em&gt;nothing&lt;/em&gt;, the reason is almost always visible in logs or terminal output.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>FAQ</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/help/faqs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 06 Oct 2025 08:49:31 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/help/faqs/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="general-questions"&gt;General Questions &lt;a href="#general-questions" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="what-is-etlx"&gt;What is ETLX? &lt;a href="#what-is-etlx" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ETLX&lt;/strong&gt; is an &lt;strong&gt;open-source, SQL-first data workflow engine&lt;/strong&gt; and an &lt;strong&gt;evolving open specification&lt;/strong&gt; for describing complete data workflows as &lt;strong&gt;executable documentation&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ETLX lets you define ETL, analytics, reporting, exports, etc using &lt;strong&gt;Markdown + YAML + SQL&lt;/strong&gt;, where the pipeline itself becomes the documentation, governance artifact, and execution plan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="what-problem-does-etlx-solve"&gt;What problem does ETLX solve? &lt;a href="#what-problem-does-etlx-solve" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;ETLX addresses common problems in modern data workflows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hidden logic spread across code, SQL, and orchestration tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Poor documentation and weak data governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tight coupling between pipelines and execution engines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Difficult auditing, reproducibility, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ETLX makes &lt;strong&gt;all logic explicit&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;self-documenting&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;auditable by design&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Authentication &amp; Access</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/auth/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/auth/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="-authentication--access"&gt;🔐 Authentication &amp;amp; Access &lt;a href="#-authentication--access" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="alert alert-warning d-flex" role="alert"&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex-shrink-1 alert-icon"&gt;
 &lt;span class="material-icons size-20 me-2"&gt;
 warning
 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="w-100"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Caution&lt;/strong&gt; — Central Set is &lt;strong&gt;production-ready and actively used&lt;/strong&gt;, but this documentation is still &lt;strong&gt;under active development&lt;/strong&gt;. Large parts of the docs are &lt;strong&gt;auto-generated&lt;/strong&gt;, evolving alongside the platform, and some sections may be incomplete, rough around the edges, or change frequently.&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Central Set Go (CSGO) provides a &lt;strong&gt;unified authentication system&lt;/strong&gt; used consistently across:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Admin UI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;REST API&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External integrations and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This section documents &lt;strong&gt;each authentication-related feature&lt;/strong&gt; with:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Applications</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/apps/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/apps/</guid><description>&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;Overview &lt;a href="#overview" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="alert alert-warning d-flex" role="alert"&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex-shrink-1 alert-icon"&gt;
 &lt;span class="material-icons size-20 me-2"&gt;
 warning
 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="w-100"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Caution&lt;/strong&gt; — Central Set is &lt;strong&gt;production-ready and actively used&lt;/strong&gt;, but this documentation is still &lt;strong&gt;under active development&lt;/strong&gt;. Large parts of the docs are &lt;strong&gt;auto-generated&lt;/strong&gt;, evolving alongside the platform, and some sections may be incomplete, rough around the edges, or change frequently.&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After a successful login, the user is automatically redirected to the &lt;strong&gt;default application&lt;/strong&gt; they have access to.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By default, this application is &lt;strong&gt;ADMIN&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Admin Schema (the DNA)</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/admin-schema/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/admin-schema/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;Overview &lt;a href="#overview" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="alert alert-warning d-flex" role="alert"&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex-shrink-1 alert-icon"&gt;
 &lt;span class="material-icons size-20 me-2"&gt;
 warning
 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="w-100"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Caution&lt;/strong&gt; — Central Set is &lt;strong&gt;production-ready and actively used&lt;/strong&gt;, but this documentation is still &lt;strong&gt;under active development&lt;/strong&gt;. Large parts of the docs are &lt;strong&gt;auto-generated&lt;/strong&gt;, evolving alongside the platform, and some sections may be incomplete, rough around the edges, or change frequently.&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;ADMIN schema&lt;/strong&gt; is the &lt;strong&gt;DNA of Central Set&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everything you see in the UI — applications, menus, tables, forms, permissions, and even automation — is defined as &lt;strong&gt;data stored in the ADMIN database&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Navigation &amp; Menus</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/menus/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/menus/</guid><description>&lt;div class="alert alert-warning d-flex" role="alert"&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex-shrink-1 alert-icon"&gt;
 &lt;span class="material-icons size-20 me-2"&gt;
