 &lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Overview</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/etlx/overview/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/etlx/overview/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;Overview &lt;a href="#overview" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Central Set was born primarily from the need to &lt;strong&gt;manage data engineering workflows&lt;/strong&gt;, but real-world data systems require much more than just pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To operate reliable data platforms, you need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User and role management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Database and schema management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forms and datatables to manage configurations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure access keys and API tokens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UI-driven configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability over pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A way to &lt;strong&gt;run data workflows reliably&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dashboards for monitoring and insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What started as a data-engineering support layer evolved into something broader.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Example</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/etlx/example/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/etlx/example/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="example---etlx--data-pipelines"&gt;Example - ETLX &amp;amp; Data Pipelines &lt;a href="#example---etlx--data-pipelines" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This page walks through a &lt;strong&gt;real-world ETLX pipeline&lt;/strong&gt;, showing how a single markdown configuration can describe:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data ingestion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transformations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data quality rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Governance artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All driven by configuration and executed step-by-step through the ETLX UI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The example uses the &lt;strong&gt;NYC Yellow Taxi - January 2024&lt;/strong&gt; dataset as a concrete and realistic scenario.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="getting-started-with-etlx-pipelines"&gt;Getting Started with ETLX Pipelines &lt;a href="#getting-started-with-etlx-pipelines" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;When you first open the &lt;strong&gt;ETLX&lt;/strong&gt; menu, the system displays an &lt;strong&gt;empty CRUD table&lt;/strong&gt;, when added pipeline its shown.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Dynamic API Reference</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/api/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/api/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="dynamic-api-reference"&gt;Dynamic API Reference &lt;a href="#dynamic-api-reference" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div class="alert alert-warning d-flex" role="alert"&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex-shrink-1 alert-icon"&gt;
 &lt;span class="material-icons size-20 me-2"&gt;
 warning
 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="w-100"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Caution&lt;/strong&gt; — Central Set is &lt;strong&gt;production-ready and actively used&lt;/strong&gt;, but this documentation is still &lt;strong&gt;under active development&lt;/strong&gt;. Large parts of the docs are &lt;strong&gt;auto-generated&lt;/strong&gt;, evolving alongside the platform, and some sections may be incomplete, rough around the edges, or change frequently.&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Central Set Go exposes a &lt;strong&gt;dynamic, context-driven API&lt;/strong&gt;.
All operations — including read-only ones — use &lt;code&gt;POST&lt;/code&gt; requests to allow rich payloads, permissions, and future extensibility.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Overview</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/dashboards/overview/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/dashboards/overview/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;Overview &lt;a href="#overview" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Central Set provides a &lt;strong&gt;first-class analytics and dashboarding layer&lt;/strong&gt; by embedding and extending
&lt;a href="https://docs.evidence.dev" rel="external" target="_blank"&gt;evidence.dev&lt;svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;&lt;path fill="currentColor" d="M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This allows you to build &lt;strong&gt;interactive analytical dashboards&lt;/strong&gt; directly on top of:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Example</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/dashboards/example/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/dashboards/example/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="analytics--dashboards--logs-dashboard-example"&gt;Analytics &amp;amp; Dashboards — Logs Dashboard Example &lt;a href="#analytics--dashboards--logs-dashboard-example" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This page walks through a real dashboard definition and explains &lt;strong&gt;how configuration, filters, metrics, charts, and tables work together&lt;/strong&gt; to produce the final analytics UI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This dashboard uses:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evidence.dev components&lt;/strong&gt; (Charts, Stats, DataTable, Inputs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CentralSet runtime&lt;/strong&gt; instead of Evidence’s native data layer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ETLX-generated datasets and Parquet files&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DuckDB WASM&lt;/strong&gt; for in-browser analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="getting-started-with-dashboard"&gt;Getting Started With Dashboard &lt;a href="#getting-started-with-dashboard" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;By default, a newly created dashboard is &lt;strong&gt;empty&lt;/strong&gt; and displays only a basic layout with an &lt;strong&gt;Edit&lt;/strong&gt; button.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Arrow Flight</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/arrow-flight/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/arrow-flight/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="arrow-flight-support"&gt;Arrow Flight Support &lt;a href="#arrow-flight-support" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="alert alert-warning d-flex" role="alert"&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex-shrink-1 alert-icon"&gt;
 &lt;span class="material-icons size-20 me-2"&gt;
 warning
 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="w-100"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important&lt;/strong&gt; – Central-Set is production-ready, but this documentation is still under active development. Large parts are auto-generated and may change as features evolve / get documented.&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3 id="overview"&gt;Overview &lt;a href="#overview" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Central-Set provides &lt;a href="https://arrow.apache.org/docs/format/Flight.html" rel="external" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apache Arrow Flight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;&lt;path fill="currentColor" d="M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; support trought &lt;a href="https://github.com/hugr-lab/airport-go" rel="external" target="_blank"&gt;airport-go&lt;svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;&lt;path fill="currentColor" d="M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; to expose analytical datasets through a &lt;strong&gt;unified, high-performance interface&lt;/strong&gt;, primarily targeting &lt;strong&gt;ETLX outputs&lt;/strong&gt;, but capable of serving &lt;strong&gt;any datasource supported by DuckDB&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>OData v4 API</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/odata-v4/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/odata-v4/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="odata-v4-api"&gt;OData v4 API &lt;a href="#odata-v4-api" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div class="alert alert-warning d-flex" role="alert"&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex-shrink-1 alert-icon"&gt;
 &lt;span class="material-icons size-20 me-2"&gt;
 warning
 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="w-100"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation status&lt;/strong&gt; — The application itself is mature and production-ready, but this documentation is still under active development. Large parts are auto-generated and continuously evolving.&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The application exposes a &lt;strong&gt;standards-compliant OData v4 API&lt;/strong&gt; that allows controlled, secure access to relational data using HTTP-based query semantics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This API is designed to be:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consumable by &lt;strong&gt;data science and analytics tools&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Easy to integrate with &lt;strong&gt;DuckDB, Python, R, BI tools&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Governed by the &lt;strong&gt;same access-control rules&lt;/strong&gt; as the UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Composable with &lt;strong&gt;ETLX workflows and metadata-driven pipelines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="endpoint-overview"&gt;Endpoint Overview &lt;a href="#endpoint-overview" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;


 
 
 

 
 
 
 

 

 &lt;div class="prism-codeblock "&gt;
 &lt;pre id="aff2bbb" class="language-http "&gt;
 &lt;code&gt;GET /odata/{db}/{table}&lt;/code&gt;
 &lt;/pre&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3 id="example"&gt;Example &lt;a href="#example" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;


 
 
 

 
 
 
 

 

 &lt;div class="prism-codeblock "&gt;
 &lt;pre id="9b97760" class="language-http "&gt;
 &lt;code&gt;GET http://localhost:4444/odata/ADMIN/menu?$filter=app_id eq 1&amp;amp;$format=json&lt;/code&gt;
 &lt;/pre&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;db&lt;/code&gt; → logical database name (e.g. &lt;code&gt;ADMIN&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;table&lt;/code&gt; → exposed table or view&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Query options follow &lt;strong&gt;OData v4&lt;/strong&gt; conventions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="supported-odata-query-options"&gt;Supported OData Query Options &lt;a href="#supported-odata-query-options" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The API supports the most commonly used OData v4 operators:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Configuration</title><link>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/config/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://realdatadriven.github.io/central-set-go/docs/tutorials/config/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="configuration"&gt;Configuration &lt;a href="#configuration" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="alert alert-warning d-flex" role="alert"&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex-shrink-1 alert-icon"&gt;
 &lt;span class="material-icons size-20 me-2"&gt;
 warning
 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="w-100"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Caution&lt;/strong&gt; — Central Set is production-ready, but this documentation is still under active development and partially auto-generated. Configuration options may expand as new capabilities are added.&lt;/p&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Central Set is primarily configured using environment variables (&lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt;).
This page documents the &lt;strong&gt;core and most commonly required settings&lt;/strong&gt; to get the platform running in development or production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💡 Tip: You do &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; need to configure everything. A minimal &lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt; is usually enough to start.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>